    "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0-beta.7 测试版\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n- 新增权威费用报价接口，报价与正式提交共用模型解析、SKU 命中、计费准备和预冻结口径；只读报价不创建任务、不冻结余额、不调用上游也不下载素材。\n- C 端模型列表新增结构化最终费用明细，Web 用户端在模型选择、素材提取、批量生成、分镜生成、编辑、高清、机位图、配音和对口型等入口展示确定或预估费用。\n- 模型 SKU 支持档位级计费口径，预冻结、结算和补退费使用实际命中档位的不可变快照；免费模型的列表价格、报价和预冻结金额统一为 0。\n- 新增可配置异步图片与视频协议，统一模型列表只读探测、JSON 或 multipart 提交、状态轮询、多参考素材装配和同源鉴权产物持久化。\n- 图片与视频任务在落库和预冻结前统一完成生成场景、输入组合、素材数量、时长、规格、比例和音画能力校验，并让任务快照、计费输入与真实下发素材保持一致。\n- 模型支持单独上传和展示 LOGO；未配置模型 LOGO 时自动回退所属服务商 LOGO。\n- 新增万相 Wan3.0 Prime 和 Wan3.0 全模态视频模型，支持文生、首帧、首尾帧及图像、视频、音频参考，按 480P、720P、1080P 配置独立 SKU。\n- 新增 Agnes Video 2.5 和 2.5 Flash 异步视频模型，支持文生、关键帧与多参考素材场景，并统一任务轮询、结果解析和计费能力。\n- 参考音频能力配置统一支持数量 `-1`、时长 `0` 和格式通配符 `*`；只有真实实现音频下发的协议才允许开启参考音频。\n- 剧本编辑新增正文哈希、编辑基线、历史版本软删除和冲突保护；自动保存支持同步空正文，手动保存继续创建新版本。\n- 批量生成按项目、剧集与逻辑任务类型原子防重，角色、场景、道具可按资产类型并行，同类任务在停止、续生和服务重启后仍保持互斥与可恢复。\n- 未登录访问首页时只返回公共内容和公共配置，登录后才合并当前用户的个人内容与状态。\n- Web 开源站点改为配置驱动的品牌标识、Favicon 和页面元信息，优化移动端访问提示、风格选择对话框、素材导入层级、跨域媒体下载、生成历史和主结果选择。\n- 修复“仅分镜脚本”模式进度不完整、创作步骤可绕过流程门禁、停止任务迟到结果继续回写，以及角色、场景、道具多层导入弹窗状态残留等问题。\n- 修复开源 Web 新手教程入口错误回退到 FAQ 的问题：仅在配置教程链接时展示，配置为空时自动隐藏，FAQ 功能保持独立。\n- 加强低资源服务器的在线源码升级治理：每个构建阶段根据实时空闲量限制 CPU 和物理内存并保留至少 15% 宿主机资源，内存压力升高时暂停或终止当前阶段；低内存 Docker 升级使用隔离的受管 Swap，失败时保留原运行版本。\n- 新增可重复执行的 `sql/v1.0.0-beta.7.sql`，补齐模型专属 LOGO 字段、Wan3.0 与 Agnes Video 2.5/Flash 模型、SKU、能力矩阵、视频功能池以及 Agnes 2.5 参考音频能力修正。新模型默认停用，请在配置密钥、确认权限与价格后再启用。\n\n\u003e 本版本为 Beta 测试版。升级前请备份数据库与部署配置，并在测试环境验证模型计费、多素材能力、批量任务恢复、剧本保存和升级 SQL。\n\n# AID v1.0.0-beta.7 Beta Release\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n- Added an authoritative billing quote API that reuses the same model resolution, SKU matching, billing preparation, and pre-authorization logic as formal submission. Read-only quotes do not create tasks, freeze balances, invoke providers, or download media.\n- Added structured final pricing details to client model lists. The Web application now shows exact or estimated costs before model selection, asset extraction, batch generation, storyboard generation, editing, upscaling, multi-view generation, dubbing, and lip-sync submission.\n- Added per-SKU metering overrides. Pre-authorization, settlement, refunds, and adjustments now use the immutable snapshot of the SKU actually selected, while free models consistently return zero list, quote, and pre-authorization amounts.\n- Added configurable asynchronous image and video protocols with read-only model probing, JSON or multipart submission, unified polling, multi-reference assembly, and safe persistence of same-origin authenticated outputs.\n- Standardized image and video capability validation before persistence and billing. Generation modes, input combinations, media counts, duration, size, aspect ratio, and audiovisual capabilities now use the same normalized request for task snapshots, billing, and provider submission.\n- Added per-model logo upload and display, with automatic fallback to the provider logo when no model logo is configured.\n- Added Wan3.0 Prime and Wan3.0 multimodal video models with text, first-frame, start/end-frame, image, video, and audio reference modes plus separate 480P, 720P, and 1080P SKUs.\n- Added Agnes Video 2.5 and 2.5 Flash asynchronous video models with text, keyframe, and multimodal reference modes, unified polling, result parsing, and billing capabilities.\n- Standardized reference-audio capability settings for unlimited counts (`-1`), unspecified duration limits (`0`), and unspecified format allowlists (`*`). Reference audio can only be enabled when the selected provider protocol actually submits it upstream.\n- Added script content hashes, editing baselines, soft deletion of historical revisions, and concurrent-edit protection. Autosave can synchronize empty content, while manual saves continue to create explicit revisions.\n- Added atomic duplicate prevention by project, episode, and logical batch-task type. Character, scene, and prop work can run independently, while conflicting work remains exclusive and recoverable across stop, resume, and service restart operations.\n- Anonymous homepage requests now return public content and public configuration only. Personal content and per-user state are merged only after authentication.\n- Updated the open Web site to use configuration-driven branding, favicon, and metadata. Improved the mobile access notice, style-selection dialog, nested asset-import dialogs, cross-origin media downloads, generation history, and main-result selection.\n- Fixed incomplete progress in storyboard-script-only mode, navigation paths that could bypass workflow gates, late result writes after task cancellation, and residual state in nested role, scene, and prop import dialogs.\n- Fixed the open Web tutorial entry incorrectly falling back to FAQ. The tutorial is shown only when a tutorial URL is configured, hidden when the value is empty, and remains independent from FAQ.\n- Hardened online source upgrades on low-resource servers. Each build stage now limits CPU and physical memory from live availability while reserving at least 15% for the host, pauses or terminates the stage under memory pressure, and uses isolated managed swap for low-memory Docker upgrades while preserving the running version on failure.\n- Added the repeatable `sql/v1.0.0-beta.7.sql` migration for the model-logo column, Wan3.0 and Agnes Video 2.5/Flash models, SKUs, capability matrices, video feature pools, and Agnes 2.5 reference-audio corrections. New models remain disabled until credentials, permissions, and pricing are verified.\n\n\u003e This is a Beta release. Back up the database and deployment configuration before upgrading, then validate model billing, multimodal capabilities, batch-task recovery, script persistence, and the upgrade migration in a staging environment.",
