  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.1.0\n\n## 中文发布说明\n\n### 新增功能\n\n- 新增案例广场完整公共链路：作品提交审核、后台审核发布与下架、不可变发布快照、公开列表与详情、成片查询、工程复制、来源追踪和复制统计。\n- 新增 TokenDance 推荐供应商接入，支持签名模型目录、协议与能力预览、幂等导入、API Key 授权、凭证版本、余额查询与提醒、充值会话和后台音色工作台。\n- 模型管理升级为统一模型、能力、协议、参数、计费与业务池配置，支持迁移预检、冲突处理、历史标识兼容、批量绑定模型池及配置版本保护。\n- 新增 GPT Image 2.5 Flare 与 GPT Image 2.5 Sunburst 图片模型基线；沿用现有 OpenAI 图片协议和有效按张 SKU，新模型默认停用。\n- 新增 Agnes 3.0 Flash 官方文本模型目录项，支持文本与图片 URL 输入、流式响应、工具调用和可关闭思考；同步更新 Agnes 官方网关、文档与价格地址，模型默认停用。\n- 分镜视频支持从本地或资产库导入单分镜参考视频，并在报价、任务快照与真实供应商请求中保持素材顺序和能力约束一致。\n\n### 优化与修复\n\n- 统一图片、视频、语音与文本任务的能力解析、素材校验、报价、预扣、路由快照、供应商错误分类和终态回写，修复多能力模型误选默认协议及合法参考素材被丢弃的问题。\n- 补齐 Wan3、Seedance、Kling Omni、MiniMax H3、Agnes Video 2.5、Vidu Multi-frame、Gemini、火山方舟等公开模型的已核验场景、参数与素材边界。\n- 修复 TokenDance 阶梯价覆盖、SKU 优先级、旧 OAuth/凭证字段兼容、授权后供应商 Key 状态、工具续轮、文本流终态及多模态路由问题。\n- 更新 DeepSeek V4 Flash 与 V4 Pro 官方价格基线，当前按高峰时段缓存未命中价格保守结算，并保留缓存命中价格元数据。\n- 后台模型管理可视化维护能力参数、调用协议和 SKU，支持直接核对价格覆盖、供应商余额与任务状态；长列表滚动、目录分页和重复请求处理得到修复。\n- 修复 Skill 草稿在未打开 Schema 页签时的空结构误判，以及关闭包含固定子 Skill 草稿时的异常。\n- Web 统一模型选择与业务参数，兼容历史模型编码和 ID；优化作品分页、参考视频导入、主图选择、导航反馈、弹窗层级、视频截帧、移动端提示及静态资源路径。\n- 修复 Gitee 内容域名跳转被可信源校验误拦截的问题，同时继续限制 HTTPS、标准端口、用户信息和重定向次数。\n\n### 数据库与兼容性\n\n- 从 `v2.0.1` 升级时执行一次 `sql/v2.1.0.sql`。脚本按依赖顺序归档案例广场、TokenDance 账户与凭证、模型配置版本、任务路由快照、统一模型能力、供应商回归修复、DeepSeek 价格、GPT Image 2.5 与 Agnes 3.0 Flash 模型迁移。\n- 增量脚本兼容 MySQL 5.7 并支持重复执行；不会写入密钥或内部网关，也不会覆盖已有合法价格、倍率、启停状态、发布状态、项目内容和同名自定义模型。\n- 新安装环境已同步 `sql/aid-init.sql`。服务端、后台管理端和 Web 需要作为同一版本同时更新。\n- 新安装基线中的智能体提示词使用中性、自包含的质量规则；现有环境升级时不会改写用户已有提示词。\n- 最低直接升级版本为 `v2.0.1`；更早版本应先按既有升级路径升级到 `v2.0.1`。\n\n### 升级注意事项\n\n- 升级前请备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录，并在维护窗口完成数据库迁移和三端更新。\n- TokenDance 凭证迁移遇到非空旧加密表会主动中止，避免把历史密文误作 API Key；请按日志提示先核对数据。\n- 新增或修正的模型默认遵循现有启停与计费配置。启用前请确认供应商权限、官方价格、网关和真实调用能力。\n- Web 更新后若仍显示旧页面，请强制刷新浏览器或清理站点缓存。\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Features\n\n- Added the complete public Case Plaza workflow, including submission, administrative review, publishing and unpublishing, immutable snapshots, public browsing, final-video access, project cloning, provenance, and clone statistics.\n- Added TokenDance onboarding with a signed model catalog, protocol and capability previews, idempotent imports, API-key authorization, credential versions, balance monitoring, recharge sessions, and an administrative voice workbench.\n- Unified model administration across identities, capabilities, protocols, parameters, billing, and business pools, with migration previews, conflict handling, legacy aliases, batch pool binding, and optimistic configuration versions.\n- Added GPT Image 2.5 Flare and GPT Image 2.5 Sunburst baselines using the existing OpenAI image protocol and valid per-image SKU settings. New models remain disabled by default.\n- Added the official Agnes 3.0 Flash text-model catalog entry with text and image-URL input, streaming, tool calling, and optional reasoning, together with current official gateway, documentation, and pricing URLs. The model remains disabled by default.\n- Storyboard video generation can now import one reference video from local storage or the asset library while preserving ordering and capability constraints through quoting and provider submission.\n\n### Improvements and Fixes\n\n- Unified capability resolution, media validation, quoting, pre-authorization, route snapshots, provider error classification, and terminal-state persistence across image, video, audio, and text tasks.\n- Completed verified scenario and input boundaries for public Wan3, Seedance, Kling Omni, MiniMax H3, Agnes Video 2.5, Vidu Multi-frame, Gemini, and Volcengine integrations.\n- Fixed TokenDance tier coverage, SKU priority, legacy OAuth and credential compatibility, provider-key synchronization, tool continuation, streaming terminal states, and multimodal routing.\n- Updated the official DeepSeek V4 Flash and V4 Pro pricing baseline. The runtime conservatively bills uncached peak input rates while retaining cache-hit pricing metadata.\n- Improved structured capability, protocol, SKU, price-coverage, provider-balance, and task-status administration, including long-list scrolling, catalog pagination, and request de-duplication.\n- Fixed Skill draft validation when schema tabs were never mounted and an editor-close failure involving fixed child Skills.\n- Updated Web model selection and business parameters with legacy identity compatibility, and improved project pagination, reference-video import, primary-image selection, navigation feedback, overlay ownership, frame capture, mobile guidance, and static asset paths.\n- Fixed trusted-source handling for Gitee content redirects while retaining HTTPS, standard-port, user-info, and redirect-count restrictions.\n\n### Database and Compatibility\n\n- When upgrading from `v2.0.1`, run `sql/v2.1.0.sql` once. It archives the Case Plaza, TokenDance account and credential, model configuration version, task-route snapshot, unified capability, provider regression, DeepSeek pricing, GPT Image 2.5, and Agnes 3.0 Flash migrations in dependency order.\n- The migration is MySQL 5.7 compatible and idempotent. It does not publish credentials or internal gateways, and it preserves valid custom pricing, multipliers, enablement, publication state, project content, and same-code custom models.\n- Fresh installations include the same baseline in `sql/aid-init.sql`. The server, admin console, and Web client must be upgraded together.\n- Agent prompts in fresh-install baselines now use neutral, self-contained quality rules. Existing user prompts are not rewritten during upgrades.\n- The minimum direct upgrade version is `v2.0.1`. Earlier deployments must first follow the existing upgrade path to `v2.0.1`.\n\n### Upgrade Notes\n\n- Back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media, then perform the database migration and three-client update in a maintenance window.\n- TokenDance credential migration stops when it finds a non-empty legacy encrypted table so historical ciphertext cannot be mistaken for an API key.\n- Verify provider access, official pricing, gateways, and real invocation behavior before enabling newly added or corrected models.\n- If stale Web content remains, perform a hard refresh or clear the site cache.",
